WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.440
Hey there, I'm Tiffany Smith for Fandango Movieclips

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:03.720
and I'm super excited

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:06.500
because London Has Fallen is coming to theaters

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:07.640
and it is the follow up,

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:09.080
No, not to White House Down

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:10.940
This is the follow up to Olympus Has Fallen.

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:13.440
In honor of the Fall of London,

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:17.160
we thought we would put together the most cinematic ways to destroy a city.

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:19.740
And of course we've got, Mother Nature herself.

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:23.520
That's right, we're talking about a good, old-fashioned natural disaster.

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:28.540
There's nothing quite like a volcano in a populated metropolitan area like Los Angeles.

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:31.960
which, I gotta say is a nice change of pace from their usual earthquakes,

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:36.260
and speaking of earthquakes, they can prove to really shake things up and knock 'em down.

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:39.160
Well, unless you've got you know, Dwayne Johnson just hanging out

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:40.600
'cuz he always saves the day.

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:44.500
Next up are our friends in the animal kingdom.

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:47.060
I gotta say you guys,  the way that we treat them,

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:49.380
I feel like we're kind of asking for it.

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:53.000
So the next time you come across a giant ape, in the wild,

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:55.760
or discover a way to bring back an extinct species,

00:00:55.760 --> 00:01:00.100
think twice, before you do something that might really tick off a giant lizard,

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:02.380
or a stampeding rhinoceros,

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:07.080
Moving along to my personal favorite, the ironic superhero fight.

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:09.340
Yes, they're just trying to save the city,

00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:13.380
but with all those powerful punches, flying bodies, and lazer blasts,

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:15.680
there's bound to be some collateral damage,

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:20.160
a pretty hefty price tag, and don't get me started on the traffic.

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:21.740
But I still love superheroes!

00:01:21.740 --> 00:01:24.560
And next on the list, we need to look to the stars.

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:26.200
That's right, I'm talking about aliens

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:30.840
and not the cute, candy eating kind that just wanna touch your finger and phone home.

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:37.600
I'm talking about the face-melting, earth-harvesting, lazer-blasting from their eyes, terrifying aliens.

00:01:38.120 --> 00:01:41.320
Whether they attack from the skies, or in their badass spaceships,

00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:45.840
or, they come through a portal on the ocean floor, they mean, business.

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:50.380
And they don't have much respect for our people, our cities, or even our really cool landmarks.

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:54.620
Alright, so that brings us to basic human stupidity.

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:59.380
That's right, our methods may be a little bit more subtle, but at the end of the day,

00:01:59.380 --> 00:02:04.420
we are just as capable of destroying our own cities and planets as any cold-blooded alien.

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:09.840
I'm Tiffany Smith for Fandango Movieclips, thanks for watching!

